  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \nHigh pressure will ensure mainly dry weather through much of \nthe week, save for an isolated thunderstorm chance across the \nhigher elevations on Tuesday. Chances of rain have gone down \neven more in the early part of next week with shortwaves around \nthe trough displaced east in more recent guidance, and scarce \ncolumn moisture to work with (forecast PWATs near the daily \nclimatological minimum). Temperatures will remain seasonable \nthrough mid- week (highs in 70s, lows in upper 40s/low 50s). \n\nTemperature uncertainty increases mid-week with ensembles indecisive \nof ridging or the stagnation of a closed low around the eastern \nseaboard. This may be the difference between remaining seasonable \n(troughing solution) or temperatures trending ~10F above average \nWednesday/Thursday (ridging solution), but most likely dry in any \nscenario.\n\nNext Friday into Saturday, confidence increases in ridging winning \nout, but there is more uncertainty in temperatures affiliated with a \ndigging surface front late-week which will also return the next \nsizable chance of any rain. CIPS also alludes this as the next non-\nzero chance of severe weather.",
